    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes, along with the full build (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented server-side assignment of a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` on owner creation.\n\n**What each change does, and why it lives there:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field with `@Column(name = \"customer_code\")` and its getter/setter. The code is owner state, so it belongs on the entity.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`). The test profile uses `hsqldb`; the rest are kept in sync so the app works on every supported database.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema (not `OwnerFields`, since it's server-assigned, not client-editable). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field, and MapStruct maps it by name automatically \u2014 no mapper edit needed, keeping `OwnerMapper` focused on display derivations.\n\n4. **New function `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 a single-responsibility step that computes the sequence (`findAll().size() + 1`, matching the existing `EnsureUniqueTelephone` pattern for reading owners) and formats `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (upper-cased first three letters + zero-padded 4-digit sequence), mutating the built owner in place. The format helper is a small private method rather than being scattered.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignCustomerCode` into the pipeline after `defaultRegistrationDate` and before `save`, under the same `transaction` governance, so the code is assigned before persistence and returned by subsequent `GET`s.\n\nBecause assignment happens within the request's transaction and before save, each created owner is counted before the next one's code is computed, giving the globally incrementing sequence the test asserts (`cb == ca + 1`).",
